    3. Pick shift s uniformly from 0..h-1. Ensure s != 0 at least sometimes for non-trivial examples.
    4. Build control column of length h: all pink(6), set row s to red(2).
    5. Prepend control column to image to form the input grid (h x (iw+1)).
    6. Output = np.roll(image, shift=s, axis=0).
